doctype html
html(lang="en")
  head
    meta(charset="utf-8")
    meta(name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1")
    title About ARENA | Sports Operations
    style.
      *{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f4f6f8;color:#17252d;font:17px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:800px;margin:8vh auto;padding:42px;background:white;border:1px solid #e0e5e6;border-radius:16px}h1{font-size:44px;letter-spacing:-2px;line-height:1.1}a{color:#245443}small{color:#60726c}code{background:#f0f3f1;padding:3px 6px;border-radius:4px}.brand{font-weight:900;letter-spacing:4px}.stats{display:flex;gap:32px;padding:20px 0;border-block:1px solid #e0e5e6}strong{display:block;font-size:30px}@media(max-width:600px){main{margin:20px;padding:24px}h1{font-size:34px}}
  body
    main
      p.brand ARENA / SPORTS OPERATIONS
      h1 Every detail behind every victory.
      p A full-stack portfolio project for managing athletes, competitions, entries and results. All seeded people and events are fictional. This project is independently designed and is not affiliated with BORNAN or FIFA.
      .stats
        div
          strong= athletes
          | Registered athletes
        div
          strong= events
          | Competitions
      h2 How it works
      p Vue 3 and TypeScript render the dashboard. Axios sends JSON requests to an Express API. Mongoose validates the records, and a storage adapter saves them to a local demo file or MongoDB.
      p This page is rendered on the server using Pug: Express combines this template with live record counts before sending HTML to the browser.
      p
        | Storage mode: 
        code= mode
        | . Demo records persist on the server between restarts.
      p Visitors can explore the workspace. Administrator sign-in is required to create, edit or delete records. This portfolio project uses fictional demonstration data.
      a(href="/") Open the operations dashboard
